{"We want the caregiver to have breaks and support so caring does not cost them their health, job or relationships.": " [supported by agi-499616, agi-499798]", "The caregiver can step away for a few hours and knows the person is looked after": " [supported by agi-499801, agi-499890]", "The caregiver can find support at times that fit a working life": " [supported by alz-77398]", "The caregiver is not the only one carrying the load": " [supported by agi-498946, agi-499890]", "We want caregivers to know what to say and do when the person is anxious, angry or confused, so visits and calls do not end in distress.": " [supported by alz-76756, alz-77460]", "A caregiver gets through a hard call or visit without a meltdown": " [supported by alz-77399, alz-77460]", "A caregiver knows when a behavior is the illness and when it needs a doctor": " [supported by alz-77399]", "Repeated calls do not take over the caregiver's workday": " [supported by alz-76894]", "We want families to understand and control money, legal papers and facility bills, so nothing is signed under pressure or paid wrongly.": " [supported by agi-499298, alz-77373]", "A caregiver knows what a facility charges and why": " [supported by agi-499732]", "A caregiver can apply for benefits without being rushed": " [supported by agi-499298]", "The person with legal authority and the relatives who help can see the same account information": " [supported by agi-499820]", "We want relatives to share the load and the information, without conflict or going through lawyers.": " [supported by alz-77412, alz-77423]", "A sibling who lives far away knows what is needed and does their part": " [partly supported by alz-77366, alz-77386]", "A relative with legal authority cannot keep others from the person without a reason they can see": " [supported by agi-499818]", "Decisions about the parent are made together": " [partly supported by alz-76894, alz-77401]", "We want the person to take their medicines, eat and stay clean without a daily fight and without the caregiver doing it all alone.": " [supported by agi-498744, agi-499433]", "The caregiver knows whether a dose was taken or missed": " [partly supported by agi-498744]", "Morning and night personal care does not exhaust the caregiver": " [supported by agi-499448]", "The person eats enough": " [supported by agi-499433, alz-77401]", "We want families to arrange a move to assisted living or a nursing home with confidence, without the person being forced or tricked.": " [supported by alz-77399, alz-77401]", "A family can compare places and costs before a crisis": " [partly supported by agi-499762, alz-77385]", "The person has a say in the move": " [supported by alz-77386, alz-77401]", "A move is planned for a time when it can go well": " [partly supported by alz-77401]", "We want the person to stay safe at home without constant watching.": " [supported by agi-499659, alz-77417]", "The caregiver knows if the person left home or fell": " [supported by agi-499433, alz-77382]", "Hazards such as the stove do not cause harm": " [supported by agi-499659, alz-77417]", "A person who wanders is found quickly": " [partly supported by alz-77129, alz-77393]", "We want families to get clear information and quick callbacks from doctors, hospitals and programs.": " [supported by agi-499762, alz-77005]", "A caregiver gets a diagnosis sooner": " [supported by alz-77385]", "A caregiver gets a callback within days, not weeks": " [no supporting quote]", "Privacy rules do not leave the caregiver without answers": " [supported by alz-77385]", "We want relatives who live far away to stay informed and able to help.": " [supported by agi-499712]", "A caregiver far away has the information the people near the parent have": " [supported by agi-499712]", "Calls and visits from far away still help the parent": " [partly supported by alz-77460]", "We want the spouse caregiver to keep their own health and have someone to lean on.": " [supported by agi-499222, alz-77379]", "The caregiver gets regular breaks": " [supported by alz-77390, alz-77406]", "The caregiver has someone to talk to": " [supported by alz-77379, alz-77427]", "The caregiver's own medical needs are not put off": " [partly supported by agi-499378, alz-77375]", "We want caregivers to handle agitation, repeated questions and refusal without anger or exhaustion.": " [supported by alz-77348, alz-77377]", "The caregiver finds something that calms the person when the usual tactics stop working": " [supported by alz-77414, alz-77449]", "Evening restlessness does not end the day in conflict": " [supported by agi-498938, alz-77406]", "The caregiver knows when to ask a doctor about behavior or medicine": " [partly supported by alz-77414]", "We want bathing, toileting, medicines and eating to be manageable at home.": " [supported by agi-499873, alz-59049]", "Night-time incontinence does not wreck the caregiver's sleep": " [partly supported by agi-499222, alz-59049]", "The person takes medicine without a fight": " [supported by agi-498938]", "Doctors can see the readings or notes the caregiver keeps": " [no supporting quote]", "We want the person to be safe when the caregiver is not with them and when they go out.": " [supported by alz-77407]", "The caregiver can leave the house briefly knowing the person is safe": " [supported by alz-77407]", "Public places work for a couple, for example restrooms": " [supported by alz-77263, alz-77410]", "A conversation about driving can happen in time": " [supported by alz-77437]", "We want caregivers to trust paid help and know what happened while they were away.": " [supported by agi-499829]", "The caregiver knows how an aide's visit went": " [supported by agi-499829]", "A hospice or aide visit happens as promised": " [supported by agi-499829, alz-77395]", "The caregiver can leave the person with others for a few hours": " [supported by alz-77263, alz-77410]", "We want families to place a spouse in memory care at the right time, in a good place, and to be able to afford it.": " [supported by agi-498938, alz-77392]", "The caregiver can judge when home care is no longer enough": " [partly supported by alz-77354, alz-77375]", "The caregiver can find a good place and pay for it": " [supported by alz-77364, alz-77392]", "Care in the new place meets the spouse's needs": " [supported by alz-77375, alz-77471]", "We want the spouse's money, bills and exposure to scams under control.": " [supported by alz-77379, alz-77411]", "The caregiver can take over bills that were left behind": " [supported by alz-77411, alz-77428]", "The person cannot be scammed or overspend": " [supported by alz-77379, alz-77411]", "Care costs can be planned": " [partly supported by alz-75137, alz-77473]", "We want a diagnosis and treatment without long waits.": " [supported by alz-77371]", "A person with new symptoms sees a specialist within weeks": " [supported by alz-77086, alz-77371]", "The family understands what is wrong": " [supported by alz-77409]", "We want family and friends to support the caregiver, not criticize.": " [supported by alz-77427, alz-77470]", "The caregiver has family who step in": " [supported by alz-77470]", "Criticism from relatives does not add to the stress": " [supported by alz-77374, alz-77427]"}